\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {STDP Depression and Potentiation evoked in each branch type.}  (\textbf  {A}) Action potentials were modeled as quadratic waveforms with variable peak amplitude to model experimental observations in the three dendritic branch sites.  (\textbf  {B}) NMDAR open-probability traces evoked by bAPs in each branch-type.   (\textbf  {C}) VGCC open-probability traces evoked by bAPs in each branch-type.   (\textbf  {D}) Integrated calcium influx in NMDARs and VGCCs evoked in each branch type. We used the GHK current equation to estimate dynamic calcium influx.  (\textbf  {E}) In STDP protocols, calcium influx through NMDARs and VGCCs leads to potentiation and depression, respectively.  (\textbf  {F}) Results from Nevian \& Sakmann (2006, reproduced from published figure via plot digitization), showing how the magnitude of potentiation and depression depend on the amplitude of calcium influx.  (\textbf  {G}) Estimated potentiation and depression evoked by STDP as a function of local bAP amplitude.  (\textbf  {H}) Predicted magnitude of potentiation and depression evoked in each branch type, using the calcium influx measured in simulations from panels A-D. }}{3}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:2}{{2}{3}{\textbf {STDP Depression and Potentiation evoked in each branch type.}\\ (\textbf {A}) Action potentials were modeled as quadratic waveforms with variable peak amplitude to model experimental observations in the three dendritic branch sites.\\ (\textbf {B}) NMDAR open-probability traces evoked by bAPs in each branch-type. \\ (\textbf {C}) VGCC open-probability traces evoked by bAPs in each branch-type. \\ (\textbf {D}) Integrated calcium influx in NMDARs and VGCCs evoked in each branch type. We used the GHK current equation to estimate dynamic calcium influx.\\ (\textbf {E}) In STDP protocols, calcium influx through NMDARs and VGCCs leads to potentiation and depression, respectively.\\ (\textbf {F}) Results from Nevian \& Sakmann (2006, reproduced from published figure via plot digitization), showing how the magnitude of potentiation and depression depend on the amplitude of calcium influx.\\ (\textbf {G}) Estimated potentiation and depression evoked by STDP as a function of local bAP amplitude.\\ (\textbf {H}) Predicted magnitude of potentiation and depression evoked in each branch type, using the calcium influx measured in simulations from panels A-D}{figure.caption.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:2@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][2][]3}{}{}{}}
